@page "/emergency-roof-repair-charlotte-nc"
@{
    ViewData["Lang"] = "en";
    ViewData["SeoEn"] = "/emergency-roof-repair-charlotte-nc";
    ViewData["SeoEs"] = "/es/reparacion-de-emergencia-techo-charlotte-nc";
    ViewData["SeoAlert"] = "Water entering now? Call before you climb.";
}
<main class="resource-site" lang="en">
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentHeader")
    <section class="resource-hero warranty-hero">
        <div class="site-shell">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Emergency roof repair Charlotte NC</p>
            <h1>Emergency Roof Repair in Charlotte, NC</h1>
            <p>If anyone is in danger, call 911 first. For an active leak, open hole or storm opening, Majestic assesses whether a safe emergency tarp can limit more water. Published tarp pricing starts at $125 for one tarp up to 20×20 ft after a safe-site check.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-gold" href="tel:+19808005991">Call (980) 800-5991</a>
                <a class="button button-ghost" href="/active-roof-leak-repair-charlotte-nc">Active leak guide</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="resource-body section" id="process">
        <div class="site-shell resource-sections">
            <article><span>01</span><div>
                <h2>What counts as a roof emergency</h2>
                <p>Tree impact, open decking, active interior water, or a large missing-shingle opening after wind. Do not walk a wet or damaged roof. Photos from the ground help. Related guides: <a class="official-link" href="/tree-roof-damage-charlotte-nc">tree damage</a>, <a class="official-link" href="/open-roof-hole-decking-repair-charlotte-nc">open hole and decking</a>.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>02</span><div>
                <h2>Tarping is temporary</h2>
                <p>A tarp is not a repair and not a claim result. Larger, multiple or steep installations are confirmed before work. Permanent repair or replacement is scoped separately after the roof is stable.</p>
            </div></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
        <div class="site-shell faq-layout">
            <div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Emergency questions</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details><summary>Do you offer 24/7 emergency roof repair?<span>+</span></summary><p>We do not advertise 24/7 coverage we cannot staff. Call the number on this page. Response is same business day when conditions allow, and sooner when a technician is available and the site is safe.</p></details>
                <details><summary>What is the emergency tarp price?<span>+</span></summary><p>$125 for one tarp up to 20×20 ft after a safe assessment. A larger standard tarp is $150. Unusual access or weather can change the plan.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Should I call the roofer or insurance first?<span>+</span></summary><p>Protect people and stop additional water when it is safe. Then document. The homeowner still files the claim. Majestic can tarp and later document construction facts.</p></details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentFooter")
</main>
